{"id": "ac1f3f37-e984-435b-b337-6107edef95bd", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll review your EBS setup in us-east-1. That covers volume types and sizing, encryption, snapshot and backup coverage, attachment state, and performance headroom. I'll report back with a readiness assessment.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_EvcACTqYwVJGgklfJSyjZ4", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-readiness-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Production-readiness review of Amazon EBS in us-east-1. Read-only: do not make any changes.",
  "context": "The user has a launch next week and wants to know whether their EBS storage is production-ready. This is a first-pass (shallow) review. Produce a concise, prioritized findings report. Agent space account is 012345678901_1; also check any other associated AWS accounts that have us-east-1 resources (use list_associations).",
  "resources": ["Region us-east-1", "Account 012345678901_1 plus any associated accounts"],
  "timeframe": "Current state for configuration; last 14 days for CloudWatch metrics (use datetime tool for timestamps)",
  "criteria": "Check and report, with volume IDs and counts: (1) Inventory: volumes by type/size/state, and which are unattached/available (orphaned/cost waste) vs in-use, and which instances they attach to (note Name tags). (2) Encryption: unencrypted volumes, whether EBS encryption-by-default is enabled in the region, and whether KMS keys are customer-managed vs AWS-managed. (3) Backup/DR: snapshot coverage and age per in-use volume (most recent snapshot, volumes with no snapshot or stale >7 days), Data Lifecycle Manager policies, AWS Backup plans/protected resources, unencrypted or public snapshots, and snapshot fast snapshot restore if used. (4) Performance/Sizing: legacy types (gp2, io1, standard) vs gp3/io2 candidates; provisioned IOPS/throughput vs actual usage; CloudWatch EBS metrics (VolumeQueueLength, VolumeReadOps/WriteOps, VolumeThroughputPercentage / BurstBalance for gp2, VolumeIdleTime) to identify saturation or burst-credit risk; instance-level EBS bandwidth limits if obvious. (5) Resilience: DeleteOnTermination flags on non-root data volumes, Multi-AZ distribution of volumes' instances, EBS-optimized on attached instances, Multi-Attach usage. (6) Monitoring: CloudWatch alarms existing on EBS volume metrics (burst balance, queue length, status checks, volume stalled IO) and any volumes with impaired status checks. (7) Tagging hygiene on volumes. Return: an overall readiness verdict (Ready / Ready with caveats / Not ready), a prioritized list of risks (High/Medium/Low) with specific resource IDs, what looks good, and any areas you could not check (e.g., permission errors)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS configuration and health in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

